id           = CWE-1395
name         = Dependency on Vulnerable Third-Party Component
abstraction  = Class
structure    = Simple
status       = Incomplete

description : The product has a dependency on a third-party component that contains one or more known vulnerabilities.

extended description : Many products are large enough or complex enough that part of their functionality uses libraries, modules, or other intellectual property developed by third parties who are not the product creator. For example, even an entire operating system might be from a third-party supplier in some hardware products. Whether open or closed source, these components may contain publicly known vulnerabilities or hidden functionality such as malware that could be exploited by adversaries to compromise the product.

notes : https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1395.html
